---
description: Flutter/Dart architecture rules
globs: flutter_app/**
alwaysApply: false
---

State management: Riverpod with code generation (riverpod_annotation +
riverpod_generator) only. Never suggest Bloc, GetX, Provider-only patterns,
or a service locator (get_it, etc.).

Error handling: use the sealed Result<T> (Success<T> / FailureResult<T>)
and sealed Failure hierarchy defined in packages/core/lib/src/domain/.
Never introduce dartz or Either. Never let a DioException or raw Response
escape a repository — map it to a Failure inside the repository implementation.

Failures carry a FailureCode enum, not a hardcoded English string.
Localized display strings are resolved in the presentation layer via
intl/ARB files, never in domain or data layers.

Package boundaries: a package may only import another package's public API
(the single lib/<package_name>.dart file), never anything under that
package's lib/src/. flutter_app/tool/verify_architecture.dart enforces this
— run it, don't just assume compliance.

Domain layer (lib/src/domain/ in any package) must never import Flutter,
Dio, json_annotation, or any platform plugin. It must be pure Dart.

Presentation layer must never call a repository or Dio directly — only
through a Riverpod provider/controller/use case. No business logic inside
widget build() methods. No network calls from widgets.

RTL/localization: use EdgeInsetsDirectional and directional icons, never
hardcoded left/right. Every user-facing string goes through ARB files for
English and Arabic — never inline hardcoded text in a widget.

Do not hand-edit generated files (*.g.dart, *.freezed.dart) — regenerate
via build_runner instead.

Do not create new feature packages unless explicitly asked. Do not scaffold
placeholder packages for future features (jobs, screening, etc.) ahead of
when they're actually being built.
